Z||000002||Big O||06-16-2000||11:24 PM||||That's my baby all right.  She needs a little shineing up, but she's running sweet and strong.  If you want to replace the powerplant in your Fiero this is definately the way to go.  Wonderful performance and reliability.  I highly recommend Chris West at West Coast Fiero if you are on the west coast or even on the west side of the Rocky Mountains.  This is not a job for a back yard mechanic and Chris does wonderful work at reasonable prices.  Mine is from a 97 Bonneville.  Get the complete powerplant including the tranny and wiring harness if you can.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dan86gt3.8||06-17-2000||03:23 AM||||Well I Have one, well minus that funny looking thing on top and I love it.  I wish I had that thing on top though I heard you car goes faster if it has one, but I don't know what thats all about.  Anyways its a great swap I HIGHLY recomend it <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000004||84 Indy||06-18-2000||12:17 AM||||Does anybody know what cars the 3.8SC series II came in? I know of the buick Roadmaster & Pontiac Bonneville. Big O is yours auto or stick?<P>[This message has been edited by 84 Indy (edited 06-18-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by 84 Indy (edited 06-18-2000).]||||reg||6
